Chimera began as a fork of BizHawk (https://github.com/TASEmulators/BizHawk),
and its code has since been written anew. What it keeps from the BizHawk
team's MIT-licensed work is the Lua functions' names and descriptions
(source/ui/viewmodel/src/lua_docs.inc), the format of a movie's input that it
reads and writes, and the names it gives keys and controls. Copyright in those
parts belongs to the BizHawk team; copyright in everything else in this
repository, apart from the exceptions below, belongs to Sergio Martin. Both
are provided under the MIT License.

Exceptions, clearly separable from the MIT-licensed sources:

- extern/ contains third-party native libraries built from source during the
  build (SDL3, Lua, zstd, SQLite, OpenAL Soft, and supporting
  projects), vendored as pinned git submodules, each under its own
  open-source license (see each submodule's license file); they are compiled
  to separate dynamic libraries loaded at runtime.
- Emulation cores are NOT part of this repository. They are loaded at runtime
  as external, self-contained packages, each carrying its own license (a core
  package derived from a GPL emulator is a GPL work, for example). Consult
  each package's own license.

The terms themselves are in LICENSE: the MIT License.
